**Definition (Entering-state subjects)** · `def:actepoch:state-subjects` The entering-state document selects separate ledger, semantic standing-basis, title, schedule, spent-slot, public-support and determination-state subjects when required by the fixed checking interpretation. Each is a subject document under (`def:actepoch:document-grade`); independent retrieval, retention and validation give the separation required by (`inv:actepoch:part-separation`). The title reference is always present, resolving to a real empty subject when its graph domain is empty. Other roles are conditional on admitted applicability rules, never producer preference. Required empty subjects are real documents, not null or zero-hash sentinels. Coverage is inline because it describes the enclosing selection rather than an independently retrieved subject. This is a designed enclosing contract, not a complete theory or an implemented reader; subject owners retain their key types, exact sufficient operands, canonical relations, limits and controls under (`open:actepoch:state-provenance`).

