Public support is the public placement state of (`def:actepoch:carried-state`), widened to retain the accepted/formed domain and public reference terms needed by anchoring, earlier references and dependent partition in (`tab:actepoch:state-checks`). It owns prior membership and placement assertions; title owns checked anchor/completion dispositions; the semantic standing basis owns cumulative contributions and per-Item, per-author revision heads, while public support resolves their public terms. Shared identities, realization references, parties and terms must agree across these subjects. Authored public parts remain separate documents. Prior formed status is an entering premise, not proof of earlier execution. Exact joins remain with records, graph and subject owners.

The complete persistent settlement-event census belongs to the semantic standing basis, including untouched Items. Title transition supplies additions; event/accepted-act identities distinguish cells and retain handshake/counterparty associations. The standing and title owners admit exact deduplication, positivity, Registration and overlap relations; an ancestor or shared Bid is not multiplied by the number of branches. On overlapping Items the event identities and parties agree with the completed title handshakes. Placing the census here pays that checked overlap join while allowing standing to read its complete cumulative basis without retrieving untouched Item graphs; placing it in title would require a full event subprojection beside every sparse graph projection.

**Rule (Coverage by subject key domain)** · `rule:actepoch:state-domain-coverage` Entering state contains one coverage manifest with an entry for each admitted key domain within each subject role. The subject admission enumerates its key domains, dependency closure and forced-full domains; every consumed global total is a full entry of its own. Each entry declares full coverage, a finite typed key domain or inapplicability under the fixed checking interpretation. Finite keys occur once in canonical order and resolve in the selected subject to a value or its admitted explicit absence case; the manifest duplicates neither values nor absence flags. An omitted finite key is outside the projection, never an absent Item, unused slot or zero balance. A full entry for a consumed total requires its value in the selected subject; an omitted total is insufficient input, never nonmembership. Nonmembership applies only to members of a full key domain. Under a full key-domain entry, omission from the complete admitted membership domain means nonmembership; it is not a missing sparse lookup. This is a supplied completeness premise, not proof of unknown historical absence. Inapplicability must follow the admitted dependency rule. Derive required domains from current acts, frame and calculation predicates, close their admitted dependencies, and check coverage; keys supplied by the producer do not define that requirement. The reason is that a role can mix sparse rows with full totals or a finite index with a full accepted domain, while all sparse domains need the same distinction between omitted support and established absence.

| Subject | What makes it touched | Required full-domain obligations despite sparse selection |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Ledger | An act’s charge/solvency predicate, a frame/gross comparison, standing emission or another required calculation reads an Actor/coordinate | All Actor-domain counts, balance/gross aggregates and other ledger totals that the selected formula consumes; emission is not determined by current acts alone |
| Public support and slots | Current acts name earlier parents, targets or slots, or another selected subject needs their public terms | Complete relevant accepted/countable closure; all spent slots needed to decide freshness, including holes; any global accepted-domain premise required by partition or standing |
| Semantic standing basis | A standing predicate reads a cell, incidence, coordinate, contribution or recipient relation, or an ordinary Owner revision or description read reads a revision head | Complete cumulative persistent event census; required per-Item, per-author revision heads; complete required contribution and normalization domains, not only endpoints of current acts |
| Title | An act or description predicate reads an Item, or standing needs its event support | Complete required Item graph and matching support for selected Items; event census remains global in the semantic basis even when no Item graph is newly touched |
| Schedule | Current pricing, safety, emission, controller or boundary check reads an in-force/pending setting | All active settings and controller memory for the selected calculation, including the required pending-to-in-force transition domain |
| Determination state | A closure/delivery predicate reads prior determination progress | The complete state of that determination subject and any cross-subject counters or aggregates its admitted transition consumes |

Exact selectors, global operands and full-domain membership meanings remain subject admissions under (`open:actepoch:state-provenance`). Network-v0.37.1 ``prop:deployment:allocation-input-completeness`` (closure) requires complete supplied projection; a numerical certificate over supplied inputs cannot establish inclusion of an omitted contribution.

**Rule (State and evidence reading)** · `rule:actepoch:state-evidence-reading` Select a held fixed interpretation and supported document theories, decode canonical envelopes and typed roles, bind references to their exact named objects, derive required operands and close subject dependencies under (`rule:actepoch:state-domain-coverage`). Check public resolution, internal relations and cross-subject joins before computing transitions. A listed finite key that its subject does not resolve is an internally inconsistent selection (Invalid), not an omission. A document whose namespace or major the reader does not hold is an unsupported theory (Unread); Invalid applies to bytes that fail a held theory. No default, earlier-epoch fetch or host cache fills a missing role or key. The reason is (`inv:actepoch:static-closure`): a successful judgment concerns the complete supplied set, not an unrecorded retrieval or producer choice.

| Situation | Reader result | What is not inferred |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Required domain, operand or consumed total omitted from the supplied selection, except a listed finite key unresolved by its subject | Insufficient supplied input, recorded as missing required public support; no static confirmation | Omitted is not absent, zero, empty or inapplicable |
| Required named document not obtainable, or a finite resource limit prevents completing the required check | Unavailable evidence/work, with the missing name or unfinished scope reported; no static confirmation | Retrieval failure or exhausted work is not a demonstrated false fact |
| Supplied bytes fail a held theory, a listed finite key is unresolved by its subject, or facts/joins contradict a held interpretation | Invalid representation or internally inconsistent state, with the failed relation named | It is not proof that a different historical state occurred |
| A required interpretation, document namespace or major is not held by the reader | Unread/unsupported interpretation; no calculation verdict | No fallback to a nearby theory or fetched mutable specification |
| Optional private opening absent | The dependent private predicate is unavailable; report the qualification alongside completed checks | Missing private evidence does not excuse missing public support |
| Explicit absence under a covered typed key | A usable entering premise if internally consistent with all public support | The local verdict does not establish historical absence; a run comparison must account for it |

These six distinctions are diagnostic results, not exit numbers or an implementation refusal order. Subject admissions fix precedence for overlapping defects. Insufficient input and unavailable evidence or work both prevent public static confirmation; an absent optional private opening qualifies only its dependent predicate. Current formation, recorded-key signature checks, pair equality, slots and counted relations are checked afresh under (`rule:actepoch:checking`); prior dispositions remain supplied premises. An accepted charged act in an incomplete handshake need not create a child and is not thereby malformed. No executed claim follows from this designed reader.

**Definition (Ledger state and result)** · `def:actepoch:ledger` Ledger state supplies the entering residual balances, cumulative counts, gross amounts and debit-vintage facts needed for current validation. Current acts and in-force inputs determine charges and outgoing values; no subsequent price reprices an earlier paid debit. History closure compares those computed coordinates with the next epoch’s supplied entering state. There is no mandatory duplicate ledger assertion inside the root, and numerical agreement does not prove chain occurrence.

**Definition (Standing result)** · `def:actepoch:standing` Standing is computed from the static semantic basis, ledger, fixed specification and selected numerical support. Independent points, instance binding and soundness support belong to V; uniquely recoverable residuals, bounds, standing and verdicts are computed without mandatory copies. Ordered required attempted-rung support remains available under network-v0.37.1 ``def:network:conserved-standing-package`` and ``post:deployment:replay-verification`` (closure). Previous standing is not another semantic solve input. realizes{``post:deployment:replay-verification``; This retains irreducible public support and recomputation in the design; no implemented numerical route or external premise is established.}

**Definition (Title state and result)** · `def:actepoch:titles` Title state supplies the undated shared Item graph, completion and counted-reference dispositions, pending and attached challenge facts for the calculation domain of (`def:actepoch:title-domain`). The complete persistent settlement-event census is carried by the semantic standing basis under (`def:actepoch:state-subjects`); title transition supplies additions and the overlapping handshake facts must agree. Its sufficient operands and transition are (`def:actepoch:title-entering`) and (`rule:actepoch:title-transition`). The current epoch computes outgoing facts; a declared run supplies dates for the named timeline read and certificate under (`def:actepoch:title-read`) and (`def:actepoch:title-summary`). Neither a global owner map nor an epoch number is title state. Concrete representation and semantic seam controls remain (`open:actepoch:title-admission`).

**Definition (Schedule state and result)** · `def:actepoch:schedule` Schedule state supplies settings in force, pending settings and controller memory. Independently selected initialization, constants and delivery observations are supplied where the fixed specification does not determine them. The static calculation computes outgoing schedules; history checks their equality to the next in-force settings, including the one-boundary lead under network-v0.37.1 ``cond:epoch:safety-publication-lead`` (closure). No stored epoch ordinal is needed for that adjacent equality. Optional proposals and trace copies are outside the root. The admitted historical-prefix reader of (`alg:design:effective-schedules`) remains until a successor is designed and built.

