**Definition (Admission and closure checks)** · `def:actepoch:admission` Static validation checks supplied accepted acts against entering facts and selected inputs. It checks formation, complete-act approval under recorded keys, pair equality, reference placement, slot freshness, charges, solvency and numerical/title predicates. Position is place in the list; logical time and key authority are not static success predicates. Missing private openings leave only their dependent checks unavailable; missing required public support prevents confirmation. Required support for unsuccessful rung attempts on the accepted set remains; entirely rejected proposed sets are not entries. The verdict concerns these data, not historical occurrence. Required public settlement and anchor support resolves inside this static set; earlier counted-reference dispositions are entering facts under (`rule:actepoch:title-prior-facts`), not earlier-epoch locators.

