**Proposition (No separate position receipt)** · `prop:actepoch:acceptance-record` A second document containing only act reference, epoch reference and position adds no independent acceptance fact once an authenticated complete acts list is available. Its tuple is a read result. The argument is that membership and order already determine that tuple. A receipt promising service or a proof allowing partial retrieval has a different subject and needs its own admission; it is not minted here as an obligatory per-act record. A copy of a witnessed act alone proves neither inclusion nor finality.

## Relations and checking · `sec:actepoch:relations`

**Invariant (Authoritative reference closure)** · `inv:actepoch:reference-closure` Every document dependency required by static checking resolves inside the epoch’s committed set. The fixed public specification is the checker’s explicit interpretation, not an external data locator. The only outward denotation is an opaque Actor name: its Actor document remains outside the set and is not opened or prefix-tested by static validation. Types and all required calculation operands resolve internally. Optional private openings and computed displays are not required public input dependencies; displays may refer inward but no root branch depends on them. The argument is that a calculation whose required inputs are all retained has no history or service dependency, and computed copies cannot be their own premises. This preserves (`inv:design:epoch-reference-authority`) and (`inv:design:optional-query-separation`).

**Invariant (Removal neutrality)** · `inv:actepoch:removal-neutrality` Removing a private opening changes no act, witness, accepted order or completed public debit, standing or title result. Removal loses an opening rather than rewriting authored data. An opening-dependent predicate may become unavailable and must be reported as such; missing required public input cannot be excused as removal or confirmed by a weaker check. This keeps (`alg:design:formation`)’s distinction and network-v0.37.1 ``post:deployment:replay-floor-scope`` (closure).

**Rule (Static closure checking)** · `rule:actepoch:checking` Read the root-selected complete static set under its identified fixed public specification, check canonical interpretation, common shapes and typed references, and resolve required documents within that set. Resolve every supplied calculation operand before evaluation: accepted act and edge records; frame Actor identifiers and gross amounts; opening ledger, semantic, title, slot, placement and schedule state; the in-force safety threshold and debit vintage; numeraire, policy-floor schedule, fixed structural-floor value and exact defining object, margin, controller formula, initialization and reduced constants; domain profiles and weights, tilt profile shape and backoff grid, depth parameters and depth mass, retention and emission parameters; boundary target size, minimum and maximum durations, announcement lead, candidate-set search policy, trial budget, timeout and fallback; arithmetic, comparison and encoding rules and each selected specification, profile and procedure version. A value determined by the fixed public source resolves there; every remaining selection resolves from core evidence or carried state, never an assumed default. This is network-v0.37.1 ``def:network:static-closure``, ``prop:deployment:allocation-input-completeness`` and ``post:deployment:replay-verification`` (closure). Check pair equality, signatures under their recorded keys, formation, slots and placement, then compute transitions, frame/ledger equations, standing, title, schedule and ordered comparison verdicts from required support. Do not open Actor documents, test name prefixes, infer key authority, read a marker or fetch a predecessor. Report “The epoch as given is internally consistent” with the completed checks and unavailable private checks and their missing operands; mandatory missing public support prevents this verdict. No computed-copy comparison or optional time assertion is a condition of static success. The ordinal-zero title condition is not claimed by this counter-free static form under (`open:actepoch:state-provenance`). realizes{``post:deployment:replay-verification``; This designs checking complete supplied static inputs and support, not external truth or implemented replay.} The title transition calculates undated branch and event facts under (`rule:actepoch:title-transition`); it does not calculate an exclusive owner or read a challenge’s prior writing epoch.

