nd its complete persistent-event census; title covers graph, completion, challenge and the revision join; schedule covers in-force/pending settings and controller memory; determination covers its required accumulated transition state. A current identity already present in the retained predecessor domain fails declared-run consistency at that seam, and the run is not accounted through that epoch; the epoch’s static verdict over its supplied set is unchanged. No tie-break chooses among colliding acts. Within an epoch and against supplied spent slots, (`rule:identity:common-document-reading`) retains the stricter local author/sequence restriction. Compare the edition-fixed payload of the selected constants edition under (`model:design:declarations`) and (`dec:decomposition:constants`), carried by the records area, for equality at every seam: the structural-floor declaration with its exact defining object and comparison procedure, numeraire, margin, formula and controller editions and reduced constants, source constant definitions, domain profiles, permitted override names, authentication realization and publication profile. This includes the floor comparison of network-v0.37.1 ``cond:epoch:safety-declared-floor`` (closure), the edition’s protocol formulas and structural constants and the supplied Actor-entry format; it does not freeze an epoch’s permitted override values, computed quantities or supplied Actor entries. The policy-floor schedule is the host’s announced setting under network-v0.37.1 ``def:epoch:policy-floor`` and ``rem:epoch:operator-authority-floor`` (closure): announced at one boundary, effective at the next, persisting until re-announced and valid only against the led threshold. Its in-force and pending values are schedule state, compared through the schedule row with the one-boundary lead, not by edition equality. The boundary target-size/minimum-duration/maximum-duration triple remains supplied boundary policy under network-v0.37.1 ``cond:deployment: