**Convention (Interface view)** · `conv:actepoch:interface` Queries expose exact static documents and typed readings under (`dec:api:schema`) and (`inv:api:document-bytes`), separately from computed displays and oracle discovery. A read manifest describes available operations and sizes without creating another authoritative set. Partial reads establish only their checked scope; full static checking requires complete public inputs without earlier-epoch fallback. Computed copies are optional courtesy answers under vendor-namespaced names, outside common documents and the root and without acceptance authority or a conformance claim, under (`rule:actepoch:computed-publication`); their consumer and name mapping remains (`open:actepoch:accountability-occurrences`). The designed successor offers a computed title reading only for a named timeline at a named evaluation point and separately lists all branches; it never returns a default winner. The service is unbuilt and awaits its own admission under (`open:actepoch:title-admission`).

